      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Eliminating Hidden Surcharges &amp; Demanding Written Binding Contracts for Transport Charge from Gorakhpur</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>When a vehicle is shipped from Gorakhpur to Delhi, the journey is usually straightforward: pick up the car, load it onto a flatbed or container, and drive to the destination. However, some unscrupulous transporters exploit this process by inserting hidden charges that only become apparent on the day of delivery.</p>
<p>These “moving‑day surcharges” are typically justified with vague terms such as “floor elevation,” “long carry,” or “toll tax.” In practice, they are a convenient way to inflate the final bill without prior notice.</p>

<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr)); gap: 20px; margin-top: 24px;">
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #f59e0b22; color: #f59e0b; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">01</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Floor elevation</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">This claim refers to the distance between the loading platform and the vehicle’s floor. Transporters may claim that the car’s height requires additional lifting equipment or a longer trailer, and then tack on a fee that is never listed in the original estimate.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #10b98122; color: #10b981; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">02</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Long carry</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Even when the route from Gorakhpur to Delhi is only about 400 kilometres, some companies add a “long carry” surcharge. They justify it by claiming that the vehicle will be driven for an extended period, but the charge is actually a disguised premium for the driver’s overtime.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #3b82f622; color: #3b82f6; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">03</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Toll taxes</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Toll fees are legitimate, but dishonest operators often add a percentage markup on top of the official toll amount. They may present a receipt that shows a higher toll cost than the government’s published rates, and then claim it as an additional expense.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<p>These tactics work because most customers rely on a verbal agreement or a simple email confirmation. Without a written, binding quote that lists every line item and the applicable rates, there is nothing to challenge when the bill arrives.</p>

<p>Transparent written binding quotes protect customers in several ways:</p>

<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>They provide a clear baseline for the agreed price, making it impossible for the transporter to add arbitrary fees later.</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Every surcharge—floor elevation, long carry, toll tax—is itemised with the exact amount, so the customer can verify that the charge is legitimate.</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>A binding contract requires the transporter to honour the quoted price, and any deviation must be documented and approved in writing.</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>In the event of a dispute, the written quote serves as evidence in a consumer court or arbitration panel.</span></li>
</ul>

<p>For a car transport charge from Gorakhpur to Delhi, a detailed, written binding quote is therefore essential. It guarantees that the customer pays only what was agreed upon, eliminates hidden costs, and ensures a fair, transparent transaction.</p></div>
